      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "We can simplify the given expression by expanding both products and then combining like terms.\n\nStarting with the first product $(2x - 5)(x + 7)$, we apply the distributive property (also known as FOIL method for binomials):\n\n\\[\n(2x - 5)(x + 7) = 2x \\cdot x + 2x \\cdot 7 - 5 \\cdot x - 5 \\cdot 7\n\\]\n\nSimplifying this, we get:\n\n\\[\n2x^2 + 14x - 5x - 35\n\\]\n\nCombining like terms:\n\n\\[\n2x^2 + 9x - 35\n\\]\n\nNow, let's simplify the second product $(x + 5)(2x - 1)$:\n\n\\[\n(x + 5)(2x - 1) = x \\cdot 2x + x \\cdot (-1) + 5 \\cdot 2x + 5 \\cdot (-1)\n\\]\n\nSimplifying this, we get:\n\n\\[\n2x^2 - x + 10x - 5\n\\]\n\nCombining like terms:\n\n\\[\n2x^2 + 9x - 5\n\\]\n\nNow, we substitute these simplified expressions back into the original problem:\n\n\\[\n(2x^2 + 9x - 35) - (2x^2 + 9x - 5)\n\\]\n\nDistribute the negative sign through the second set of parentheses:\n\n\\[\n2x^2 + 9x - 35 - 2x^2 - 9x + 5\n\\]\n\nNow, combine like terms:\n\n\\[\n(2x^2 - 2x^2) + (9x - 9x) + (-35 + 5)\n\\]\n\nSimplifying further:\n\n\\[\n0 + 0 - 30\n\\]\n\n\\[\n-30\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the simplified form of the given expression is:\n\n\\boxed{-30}",
